WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.502
Ukraine's first lady, Olena Zelenska,

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.471
opened the World Economic Forum

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.638
in Davos, Switzerland,

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.775
with this stark warning.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.177
---

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.412
---

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.047
We are facing the threat

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.383
of a collapse of the world as we know it.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.084
The way that we are accustomed to it

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.553
or to what we aspire

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.921
this war can go further

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.223
and make crisis wider

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.393
if the aggressor does not lose.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.560
This while back home

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.662
her people suffer stepped up horrors.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.063
And mass

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.298
killings by the aggressor Russia.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.933
The number of residents

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:34.968
killed by a cruise

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.770
missile strike on their apartment

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.971
block in De Dnipro

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.540
has now risen to at least 45 people,

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.542
something her husband, President

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.710
Volodymyr Zelensky,

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.545
has called a war crime.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.747
Russia's war in Ukraine is topic

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:48.314
number one

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:48.815
at the Davos

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:49.983
summit Leaders,

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.384
of course, will also discuss

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.185
climate change

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.820
and the cost of living crises.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.588
But will the forum be

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.624
more than just a talking shop?

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.160
One voice carries a lot of weight.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.729
My first guest, European Commission

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.864
President Ursula von der Leyen,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:05.732
recently named

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.534
the most powerful woman in the world

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.968
by Forbes magazine.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:09.602
She joined me

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.504
right after delivering a speech

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.706
that was designed to spur action

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.842
and to speed up support to Ukraine.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.078
President von

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.979
der Leyen, welcome to the program.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.815
Thank you very much for having me.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.349
Can I ask you your assessment?

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.884
I know your speech was devoted

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.120
a lot to the war in Ukraine.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.889
Russia has had some maybe symbolic

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.524
psychological successes,

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.993
particularly around solidarity, etc.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.429
and it has stepped up its war

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.464
against civilians.

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:40.066
The terrible death of at least 40 people

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.136
from a residential attack in De Dnipro.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:44.871
How do you assess

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.306
do you think Russia is getting back

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.373
onto the front foot

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.309
or still on the back foot?

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.044
I think Russia is still on the back foot

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.479
because first of all, Russia

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.880
never accounted

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.715
for the incredible courage

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.750
of the Ukrainian people

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.220
and Russia never accounted

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.555
for the strong support

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.423
the international

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.191
community would give Ukraine.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:06.893
The European

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:07.861
Union is supporting

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.329
with whatever it takes

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.230
Ukraine

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.464
because we know that Ukraine

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.466
is not only fighting against Russia

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.668
and for its sovereignty and integrity

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.003
of its territory,

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.638
but also for the respect

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.373
for the international law

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.242
and the fundamental rights.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.811
And therefore, we are deeply concerned.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.146
Whatever it takes,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.014
we have to support Ukraine.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.315
So those are great words.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.083
And for sure,

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.918
the EU and NATO partners,

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:32.619
the United States,

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.187
have done a huge amount.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.722
But we're hearing from everybody,

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.791
including beleaguered Ukrainian soldiers,

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.793
that is just not enough

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.795
for this onslaught right now.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.397
They still don't have the air

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.331
defense systems.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.833
They still don't have all the artillery

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.002
or the ammunition that they need.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.337
And this is what Olena Zelensky,

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.505
the first lady,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.440
told you all at Davos today.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.777
You're all united by the fact

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.380
that you are really very influential

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.081
---

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.249
But there's also something

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.118
that separates you

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.353
--- and  that, is

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:08.454
that not

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.924
all of you are using this influence,

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:11.925
---

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.259
or sometimes

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.727
you use it in a way

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:17.130
that divides even more so.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:17.997
President von

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:18.331
der Leyen,

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.666
that's a pretty strong,

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.935
frankly, accusation

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.102
from a grateful nation,

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.437
it has to be said.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.305
And we know

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:26.906
that there is a race against time.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.408
And we know that there's an argument

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.310
in your country, Germany.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.312
You're a former defense minister.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:35.048
Do you believe that the German chancellor

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:39.052
should deliver the leopard tanks to join

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.553
what other European countries

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.155
are doing now?

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:44.390
As you know, the European level,

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.858
the European Union does not own

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.193
any military capability.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:47.794
But I've said

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:50.263
from the onset of this atrocious war

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.432
that Ukraine

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.500
should get all the military equipment

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.569
it needs and it can handle

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.071
And this also includes

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.472
the advance system.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.607
So I hope very much

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:02.842
that in Ramstein, when the meeting is

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.944
I think it's the 21st of January

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.680
that there will be a big move forward

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.815
and the decision taken

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:11.451
that is so necessary overall.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.152
Ukraine

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.153
also says

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.256
that it has gotten a lot of support

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:16.756
and that is good.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.992
So but yes, there has to be

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.260
we need to step up in that.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:21.995
Do you

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:22.962
I mean, again, you're

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.564
the former defense minister of Germany.

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:25.531
I know you're currently

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.267
the president of the European Commission.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.869
But, you know, Chancellor Schultz,

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:31.137
you know these people.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.372
Will you be urging him

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.673
to make that decision

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.108
on behalf of Europe

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.210
and on behalf of what you all say

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.479
is to defend Ukraine to the end,

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.681
that Putin must win

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.882
and that your credibility

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.018
is on the line right now?

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:47.920
Yeah, but I do not have to convince

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:49.856
the head of state and government

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.958
because they know that.

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:52.992
Of course,

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.727
we talk a lot about this topic.

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:55.595
It has been,

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:56.262
for example,

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.597
every time a subject

00:04:57.597 --> 00:05:00.133
that the European Council and indeed

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.835
there is a need to step up.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.137
Now, the deliveries

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.872
we just made

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:06.939
the decision

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:07.907
that we will deliver

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:12.078
€18 billion in 20, 23 financial support.

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:13.579
That is the responsibility

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.581
for example of the commission.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:19.352
Yesterday we dispatched the first tranche

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.687
of 3 billion

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:22.855
for the month of January and February.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:25.024
So in many different urgent fields

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:26.826
we are stepping up.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:27.794
And again,

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:30.863
I think Ukraine should get that material

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.799
it needs and it can handle.

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:34.334
I want to ask you about sanctions

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.202
because again you've been very clear.

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.203
You've done sanctions

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.972
after sanctions against against Russia.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.074
But we are hearing

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.942
and I'm sure you've seen the reports

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.677
that despite that,

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.746
a lot of these proscribed

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.281
proscribed goods

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.116
are actually getting through by road,

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:51.184
and especially

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:52.585
according to latest reports

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:54.721
from the country of Georgia,

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:56.689
How does one stop Russia getting

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.391
what is what it needs,

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:00.293
even under sanctions?

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:01.494
Yes, we have issued

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.229
nine rounds of sanctions

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:05.765
and these sanctions are biting.

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.533
They are crippling the Russian economy

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:08.201
and starving

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:10.603
at all of the modern technologies

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:11.938
that is working.

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:15.641
But we also see that, of course, there is

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:17.343
the attempt

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:18.511
of circumvention

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.713
and we cannot accept that.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.149
We have already started to say

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.083
that we are going to list

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:26.753
those people who take technologies

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:27.153
or goods

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.721
from the European Union

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.823
and bring them into Russia.

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:33.893
But the 10th package of sanctions

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:36.095
will be mainly focused

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:38.865
on closing these loopholes, on

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.701
finishing off with these circumvention

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:45.271
and having massive consequences for those

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:46.739
who circumvent

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.274
the sanctions of the European Union.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:50.443
So the 10th package will be on that.

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:52.412
You just mentioned the United States and

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:53.946
and Washington is watching

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.215
you and your speech very closely.

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:57.150
There's a U.S.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.485
delegation there in Davos.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:00.820
You are meant to be having a meeting.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.288
I don't know whether you did

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:05.191
to try to calm your fury

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:07.827
at what you call protectionism

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:08.060
or what

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.128
European nations

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:10.596
are calling protectionism

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:14.167
because of the US you know, the I.R.A.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.869
law, the inflation reduction

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:17.703
bill,

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:20.106
you're very worried about your car sector

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.541
and others, main countries

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:22.942
like France and Germany are very,

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:23.876
very worried.

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:26.779
Is there any resolution to that?

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:28.781
And do you see it happening?

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:30.249
Yes.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:30.750
Well, first

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.050
of all, I

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.219
must say we welcome

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:34.520
that there is the Inflation

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.188
Reduction Act,

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:37.957
which is basically massive investment

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:39.992
in the green transition. That's good.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.127
Let's join forces

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.829
there as you know, the European Union

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:44.464
has its European Green Deal

00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:45.898
and our massive investment

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:47.400
program of 800 billion

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.901
for next generation EU.

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.269
So it is good

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:52.905
that the US are also stepping up

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:55.441
their investment in the green transition.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:59.378
There's one point where we have to go

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:00.813
into deeper discussions

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:01.948
and that is

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:04.350
we want to compete on quality,

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:05.618
but there needs to be

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:07.153
a level playing field.

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:08.120
And therefore, indeed,

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.022
I am working with the United States

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:11.123
on an agreement

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:12.358
that these investments

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:14.293
on both sides of the Atlantic

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:18.197
should be a joint effort to bring forward

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:19.999
the clean tech industry

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:22.034
to boost the clean tech industry.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:24.237
And on our side, on the European Union,

00:08:24.337 --> 00:08:26.639
we will come forward

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.741
with a Green Deal industrial plan,

00:08:29.141 --> 00:08:31.878
which basically looks at what can we do

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:33.646
in a regulatory environment

00:08:33.646 --> 00:08:36.549
to speed up the deployment of clean tech?

00:08:36.983 --> 00:08:39.452
What can we do in the

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:42.855
on the field of funding and state aid?

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:46.225
What do we have to do for skilling people

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.761
and how can we improve trade

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:49.562
for the clean tech?

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:51.597
So this is the Green Deal

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:52.465
Industrial Plan,

00:08:52.465 --> 00:08:56.102
which is basically the answer to the IRA.

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:57.870
And as I said, we work

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:58.905
with the United States

00:08:58.905 --> 00:09:00.039
to have a real level

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:00.806
playing field,

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:02.642
to compete on content,

00:09:02.642 --> 00:09:04.544
on substance, on quality

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:06.279
for the clean tech sector.

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:08.281
We need the Senator Joe Manchin.

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:08.514
You know,

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:09.081
the centrist

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:11.450
Democrat says that EU worries

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:15.121
were overwrought and hyper hypocritical.

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:16.822
And he's already told the French

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:17.823
president

00:09:17.823 --> 00:09:20.593
that the IRA could never hurt Europe.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.161
What is your response to that?

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:25.531
Well, I like

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:27.733
this mutual understanding

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:29.735
that we are in this fight

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:31.604
against climate change together

00:09:31.604 --> 00:09:32.705
and that we know

00:09:32.705 --> 00:09:35.174
crucial will be the clean tech industry,

00:09:35.508 --> 00:09:38.277
wind power generation, solar panels

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:40.313
hydrogen is very important.

00:09:40.313 --> 00:09:41.113
All these topics

00:09:41.113 --> 00:09:42.481
we have to bring forward.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:43.816
We need a lot of innovation.

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:45.751
We need a lot of boosting

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:47.086
of this clean tech industry.

00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:49.889
We need secure supply chains.

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:51.357
So we also have to

00:09:51.357 --> 00:09:52.491
look into the question,

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:53.192
where do we get

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:54.060
our rare earths

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:56.162
from the critical raw materials?

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:57.063
For that,

00:09:57.063 --> 00:09:58.064
we also will do

00:09:58.064 --> 00:09:58.931
the critical Raw

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:00.499
Materials Act,

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:02.234
which is creating a club

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:04.270
of like minded countries

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.639
to have these secure supply chains.

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:09.275
So if this is the mutual understanding

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:11.577
we have on both sides of the Atlantic,

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:14.146
I'm not at all worried, but very positive

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:15.147
that will be

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:16.248
we will be leading

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:17.984
in this green transition to the

00:10:17.984 --> 00:10:19.418
green tech industry.

